SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rede von Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz beim Internationalen Gedenktag der Unesco an die Opfer des Holocaust am 27. Januar 2022","publisher":"Bundesregierung","publication_date":"2022-02-01","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/service/newsletter-und-abos/bulletin/rede-von-bundeskanzler-olaf-scholz-2002388","claim":"Scholz said antisemitism, hate speech, hate against Israel, and violence against Jews were increasing, insisted that antisemitism has no place in Germany, and warned that free societies must not let extremists take control; he also referred to protesters wearing yellow stars marked 'unvaccinated' as a distortion of Holocaust memory.","locator":"lines 203-206","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary contemporaneous Scholz speech; strong direct ruler attribution for incitement and anti-hate posture.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to incitement, minority protection, and crisis rhetoric.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz speech and framing; not inherited context.","contrary_evidence":["A speech is not the same as enforcement or remedy.","The source shows stance more than measurable protection outcomes."],"lenses":["3B.3","3B.6","3B.8","3B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Federal Chancellor Scholz visits arrival centre in Berlin-Tegel","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-04-05","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-en/service/archive/arrival-centre-tegel-2023894","claim":"On 4 April 2022 Scholz visited Tegel, which had become a central arrival and registration point for people fleeing Ukraine; the registration process helped refugees obtain accommodation, work permits, and free language courses.","locator":"lines 181-196","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government visit note with concrete service details and dated ruler presence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to refugee protection and domestic crisis management.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Scholz's public prioritization of refugee reception, though delivery depended on federal and Land administration.","contrary_evidence":["This is a visit and service description, not evidence of nationwide effectiveness.","The underlying refugee influx was inherited from Russia's invasion of Ukraine."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rede von Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz bei der Online-Geberkonferenz 'Stand up for Ukraine'","publisher":"Bundesregierung","publication_date":"2022-04-11","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/service/newsletter-und-abos/bulletin/rede-von-bundeskanzler-olaf-scholz-2025152","claim":"Scholz said Ukrainian refugees were welcome in Germany and that the federal government, Länder, and municipalities would ensure shelter, medical care, schooling, and a safe future; he also announced additional humanitarian support.","locator":"lines 195-197","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary dated Scholz video statement with explicit protection commitments.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 during the refugee-response phase of the Ukraine war.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz commitment, though implementation was shared across levels of government.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian promises do not guarantee actual delivery.","The source concerns refugees from an external war, not ordinary domestic crime."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Deutschland 2022","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2023-03-28","url":"https://www.amnesty.de/informieren/amnesty-report/deutschland-2022","claim":"Amnesty reported that inadequate investigations into discriminatory identity checks (racial profiling) violated non-discrimination rights, and that the lack of an independent complaint mechanism continued to block justice and remedy for police abuse.","locator":"lines 115-117","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Major rights NGO annual report summarizing 2022 with specific remedy and oversight findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers the full 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Government-level responsibility is indirect and structural rather than a single Scholz order; the report reflects federal and state policing institutions under his chancellorship.","contrary_evidence":["The report does not prove Scholz personally ordered the abuses.","Open, litigated remedies still exist in the German system, but Amnesty says they were insufficient."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"BASU v. Germany","publisher":"European Court of Human Rights","publication_date":"2022-10-18","url":"https://hudoc.exec.coe.int/eng?i=004-62530","claim":"The Court found that Germany failed to ensure through an independent body an effective investigation into an arguable racial-profiling allegation involving a federal police identity check, and found the internal investigation insufficiently independent.","locator":"HUDOC case description and judgment summary","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Binding judicial finding from the ECHR; strong independent corroboration of oversight failure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and highly relevant to policing oversight during the year.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Germany's law-enforcement and judicial framework during Scholz's term, not a personal order from Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["The incident predated Scholz's chancellorship, though the legal failure was judged in 2022.","The case concerns a specific identity check, not the whole policing system."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4","3B.5"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Deutschland 2022","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2023-03-28","url":"https://www.amnesty.de/informieren/amnesty-report/deutschland-2022","claim":"Amnesty reported that a May 2022 Federal Administrative Court ruling confirmed that protest camps and their necessary infrastructure are protected by assembly rights.","locator":"lines 129-130","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Major rights NGO annual report citing a court ruling and summarizing its domestic-safety significance.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers 2022 and directly concerns protest protection.","ruler_attribution":"This reflects the constitutional and judicial environment under Scholz rather than a personal order, but it matters for ruler-period protection judgments.","contrary_evidence":["Protection exists at the legal level, not necessarily in every policing practice.","The cited court ruling is not itself a Scholz initiative."],"lenses":["3B.8","3B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Deutschland 2022","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2023-03-28","url":"https://www.amnesty.de/informieren/amnesty-report/deutschland-2022","claim":"Amnesty said some protests were disproportionately restricted, including a June 2022 limit of only 50 demonstrators at the Germany-hosted G7 site.","locator":"lines 130-131","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Major rights NGO annual report with a concrete restriction example and target-year fit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 protest practice.","ruler_attribution":"This is partly attributable to federal hosting and security policy under Scholz, but the immediate decision was operational and intergovernmental rather than solely personal.","contrary_evidence":["A security restriction at a G7 summit is not proof of generalized repression.","The report gives one concrete example rather than a nationwide pattern."],"lenses":["3B.5","3B.8","3B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Deutschland 2022","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2023-03-28","url":"https://www.amnesty.de/informieren/amnesty-report/deutschland-2022","claim":"Amnesty reported that in August 2022 police in Dortmund fatally shot a 16-year-old Senegalese refugee with multiple rounds from a machine gun, and that criminal investigations were still ongoing at year-end.","locator":"lines 120-123","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Clear annual-report documentation of a serious police use-of-force case and ongoing investigation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This was a state-police incident under Scholz's chancellorship, but it was a state-level operational event rather than a federal order.","contrary_evidence":["The report does not establish Scholz personally directed the shooting.","This is a single grave event, not by itself evidence of a nationwide terror pattern."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nach Razzia gegen 'Reichsbürger' Scholz besorgt über Verbindungen zur AfD","publisher":"tagesschau.de","publication_date":"2022-12-08","url":"https://www.tagesschau.de/inland/razzia-reichsbuerger-staatsstreich-geplant-107.html","claim":"After the Reichsbürger raids, Scholz said Germany has a resilient state and a militant democracy and that the security authorities can thwart such violations; the raids themselves led to 25 arrests in a far-right coup plot case.","locator":"lines 154-156","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous independent reporting with direct Scholz quotation and clear event context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in late 2022 and relevant to crisis response and domestic extremist threats.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz public response to a domestic security threat; the raid was executed by security services rather than personally by him.","contrary_evidence":["The quote reflects rhetoric after enforcement, not prior prevention.","The plot was a policing/intelligence success, but the article does not prove Scholz personally ordered it."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.6","3B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Report 2023: Germany","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-12-12","url":"https://www.hrw.org/world-report/2023/country-chapters/germany","claim":"HRW reported that police were doing too little to prevent racism and antisemitism inside the police, noting that police training addressed the issue in only 5 of 16 federal states and that independent complaint bodies existed in only seven states.","locator":"lines 73-73","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent annual human-rights review citing a specific study and summarizing structural oversight deficits.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers 2022 conditions and provides structural context for the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Structural and multi-level responsibility under the Scholz chancellorship; not a single-person act.","contrary_evidence":["The finding is study-based and not a direct audit of federal command.","State-level variation limits direct federal attribution."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Germany: Freedom in the World 2023 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2023-03-09","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/germany/freedom-world/2023","claim":"Freedom House said that in December 2022 German security services conducted raids in more than 150 locations and arrested 25 people affiliated with the Reichsbürger movement, which it described as a far-right terrorist group accused of plotting to violently overthrow the government.","locator":"Key Developments in 2022, lines 83-85","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Well-known country report with a concise 2022 summary and direct incident description.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Summarizes the 2022 year directly.","ruler_attribution":"This is state/security context under Scholz rather than personal conduct, but it informs the domestic-threat baseline.","contrary_evidence":["A country report is a summary, not an operational record.","The raids show enforcement capacity more than routine protection quality."],"lenses":["3B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across official German government speeches, ECHR legal records, Amnesty and HRW annual reports, Freedom House country coverage, tagesschau reporting, BKA/Interior Ministry material, and various Reuters mirrors.

Kept:
- Scholz speeches on Holocaust remembrance, refugee protection, and anti-hate response
- the Tegel refugee-center visit
- Amnesty and ECHR material on racial profiling, complaints, protest rights, and police violence
- the Reichsbürger raid and Scholz’s response
- HRW and Freedom House context for police-oversight gaps and the December 2022 extremist threat environment

Rejected as duplicate or weak:
- multiple Reuters mirrors of the same Reichsbürger raid or refugee statements
- 2023-2026 retrospectives that repeated 2022 facts without adding materially new detail
- generic Germany democracy summaries that were too broad when a more specific Amnesty, HRW, or court source existed
- sources about Ukraine or foreign policy that did not create a direct domestic-safety nexus
- protest-law material that did not clearly link to the federal chancellorship or repeated the same assembly-rights point already covered by Amnesty

**Remaining gaps**
- The evidence is strong on anti-incitement, refugee protection, protest rights, and oversight defects, but thinner on direct Scholz-authored domestic-safety reforms in 2022.
- I do not have a clean federal source showing a Scholz-led package specifically fixing police complaint mechanisms, racial profiling, or extremist infiltration in security services during 2022.
- The most serious adverse incident I found is the Dortmund police killing, but it remains a state-police event; the federal attribution is partial.
- I did not find a target-year source showing Scholz personally used emergency powers or coercive domestic controls in a way that materially changed the band.
- More search would help mainly on one point: whether Scholz or his cabinet took any concrete 2022 federal steps on police oversight, anti-racism in policing, or minority protection that go beyond speeches and general rights framing.
